%T A399817 745125628983219
%N A399817 Number of labeled simple graphs G on n vertices whose open-neighborhood hypergraph is Hausdorff.
%C A399817 The open neighborhood of a vertex v of a simple graph G is N(v) = {w : {v,w} is an edge of G}. The graph G is neighborhood-Hausdorff if, for every two distinct vertices x,y, there exist vertices u,v such that x is in N(u), y is in N(v), and N(u) intersect N(v) is empty.
%H A399817 Vladeta Jovovic, <a href="/A399817/a399817.pdf">Note on Neighborhood-Hausdorff Graphs</a>
%e A399817 a(5)=12: the only neighborhood-Hausdorff graph on 5 vertices up to isomorphism is C_5, which has 5!/|Aut(C_5)| = 120/10 = 12 labeled copies.
%K A399817 nonn,more,new
%O A399817 0,5
